    "narrative": "For the August 22nd slate, our top-tier offensive output centers on the corner infield duo of **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and **Gunnar Henderson** (63.26), both of whom capitalize on a high-ceiling matchup against McClanahan. While the 41% rain risk in their venue necessitates monitoring, their base projections are significantly buoyed by favorable park factors (+16%). Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.15) remains a pillar of the lineup, successfully navigating a difficult matchup against Weathers due to strong platoon splits (+7%) and a prime spot in the two-hole. These three players represent our most reliable paths to runs and RBI production today.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved determining the final utility spot between **Miguel Vargas** and the lower-scoring **Heliot Ramos** (43.98). While **Miguel Vargas** posted a stronger overall score (47.82) based on his solid 0.382 xwOBA and favorable wind conditions, the strategy for the Austin Waves remains fixated on our scarcity needs. **Nasim Nunez** (45.85) remains locked into the starting lineup specifically for his speed profile, as we must maintain our edge in the SB category regardless of his suboptimal batting order placement. **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) also merits a start over higher-projected alternatives because he provides a vital speed contribution, even while facing the \"Elite Hold\" pressure against Kremer. \n\nBeyond the weather-impacted trio, we are tracking the performance of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (52.67) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (53.84) closely. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is squaring off against the elite arm of Cease, requiring him to rely on his dynamic platoon advantage to overcome the pitching skill deficit. We continue to manage our bench depth carefully, as **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Josh Jung** remain sidelined. Depth pieces like **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White** remain on standby, though none possess the requisite profile to displace our current starters. We will proceed with the active roster as structured, prioritizing speed and high-leverage counting stats while keeping a close eye on any late-inning weather delays.",
